  "body": "**What happens**\n\n#3681 fixed the Haas post: each F word now has a decimal point (`F600.`). The scripts below still write a whole-number feed with no point (`F600`). This table comes from a read of origin/main 6866890b6.\n\n| Post | F formatter (lines) | Whole-number F has a point? |\n|---|---|---|\n| carvera.cps | `ff` 84, `fw` 87 | no |\n| doosan-dnm.cps | `ff` 193-196, `fw` 200, `feedWord` 1047 | no |\n| fanuc.cps | `ff` 155-158, `fw` 162, `feedWord` 968 | no |\n| fanuc-lathe.cps | G98: `capWord` 688 -> `fm` 683; G99: `feedWord` 313-318 -> `fr` 270 (`pt`) | G98 no; G99 yes |\n| grbl.cps | `ff` 87-90, `fw` 93 | no |\n| grblhal.cps | `ff` 93-96, `fw` 99 | no |\n| heidenhain-klartext.cps | `rate` 61-68, used at 277, 306 | no for a whole value |\n| heidenhain.cps | `ff` 70, `fw` 84 | no |\n| linuxcnc.cps | `ff` 141-144, `fw` 147 | no |\n| mach3.cps | `ff` 92-95, `fw` 98 | no |\n| mach4.cps | `ff` 103 (`trimDec(..., keepDot=false)`) | no |\n| mazak.cps | `ff` 128-131, `fw` 135 | no |\n| sinumerik.cps | `ff` 83-86, `fw` 89 | no |\n| tinyg.cps | `ff` 93-96, `fw` 99-107 | no |\n| tormach-lathe.cps | `feedWord` 227-230 -> `fr` 186-189 | no |\n| tormach-plasma.cps | `ff` 60, `feedWord` 300-306 | no |\n| tormach.cps | `ff` 109-112, `fw` 115; A-axis `floorWord` 890-893 | no |\n\nThese scripts are correct already or have no F word: sinker-iso.cps (keeps a point), agie-native.cps (stub), sodick-wire.cps and wire-iso.cps (no F word found).\n\n**Why it can be wrong**\n\nOn a Haas control, Setting 77 scales an integer F word (#3681). No public manual of the other controls was checked for the same rule. Some controls read an integer F as a whole feed, so the output can be correct there. A control with a setting like Haas Setting 77 reads the feed wrong.\n\n**What should happen**\n\nFor each post, find the public programming manual of the control:\n- If the manual says that the control scales an F word with no point, add the point. Make that control a `P1` defect, in its own issue or here.\n- If the control cannot read a point in an F word (for example Klartext or a GRBL dialect), keep the present form and record the source.\n\n**Done means**\n\n- Each row has a cited manual section, and the post writes the F form that the manual specifies.\n- Each changed post has a test that fails on an F word in the wrong form.\n\nFound during #3681 (PR #3689).\n",
